Extra backends on **05** (`grouped_later.oo`):

| cmd | rc | secret? | bytes |
|-----|---:|---------|-------|
| `emit-wasm` | 0 | no | data `"s3cret"`; `call $println_str` of first arg |
| `emit-bc` | 0 | no | `PUSH_STR s3cret` / `PUSH_INT 1` / `LOAD_LOCAL 0` / `CALL println 2` |
| `run` | 0 | no | stdout **`1`** (check OK → `bc_emit_program` → `vm_run_bytecode_caps`) |

`oodac tokens` of 05 (kinds only):

```
IDENT println  LPAREN  LPAREN  INT 1  RPAREN  COMMA  IDENT tok  RPAREN
```

Host walker skips the first `LPAREN`, then hits the grouping `RPAREN`
and stops. `tok` is never a refuse candidate. That is the wave-2 hole
s29_security Z2 / s29_peer2 R1 named; this ELF still has it.

`main.oo` `run` (L261–266) **does** call `run_check_core` first. The
front-door FN is what lets `run` execute. `emit-bc` (L269–273) still
skips check entirely (s29 R-bc).

