3. Source (WT) — what a rebuild *would* run
---

`check_secret_println_sinks` L173–200 (WT; **not** in this ELF):

```
if sid == "println" || sid == "eprintln" {
    … optional one LPAREN …
    let mut depth = 1;
    while in_args && p < n {
        if tk == "LPAREN" { depth = depth + 1; p = p + 1; }
        else if tk == "RPAREN" {
            depth = depth - 1;
            if depth <= 0 { in_args = false; }
            p = p + 1;
        } else if tk == "IDENT" {
            c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved(env, sid, nm);
            …
```

`c_secret_scan_call` L97–113: same depth; `COMMA` only if `depth == 1`.

**Still no** `c_secret_emit_guard` in this file (grep **none**). Wave-2
is not DE2.9. After a rebuild, check / llvm / wasm / run / emit-c
**front-door** should refuse 05/06/08/09. Stmt `c_emit_println` stays
flat — emit-bc (no front-door) would still leak 09.

`c_emit.oo` L86 / `llvm_emit.oo` L79 / `check_drive.oo` L62 still
call `check_secret_println_sinks`. WT `check_drive` is secret-**before**
type (6.1). ELF `run_check_core` is still secret-**after** type
(s29 R-check-order). Not wave-2, still stale.

---
4. Runtime (`chs_rt`) — not a SECRET host
---

`chs_rt_print.c`: `oo_print_str` / `oo_println` / `oo_eprintln` write
stdout/stderr. **No** taint, **no** `ERR\tsecret`.

`grep` of `ooda/runtime/*`: **zero** `c_secret*` / `__sec__` /
`refuses SECRET`. SECRET dies at emit/check, before gcc / the VM
print floor. `oodac run` of 05 printing `1` is a **front-door miss**,
not a runtime seal miss.

